3. Simplified the component structure
4. Injected the mocked hooks directly into the window object
5. Ensured all necessary data is available before rendering
6. Properly structured the mock data to match what the component expects

The key changes are:
- Using a HOC pattern to inject dependencies
- Ensuring the router query is available immediately
- Simplifying the overall structure
- Making sure all required data is mocked properly

This approach should resolve the Zod validation error by ensuring the `id` parameter is available when the component needs it.

